</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Complementary and Alternative Medicine: a Japanese Perspective</article-title><source>Evid Based Complement Alternat Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15480436</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ecam/neh029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fukawa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><source>Public health insurance in Japan</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Washington, DC: World Bank Institute</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nomura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakayama</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Japanese healthcare system</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2005</year><volume>331</volume><fpage>648</fpage><lpage>649</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16179678</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.331.7518.648</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uemura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Heterogeneity among complementary and alternative therapies- results of a survey of outpatients in Japanese general practices</article-title><source>Journal of Kyoto Prefectural University of Medicine</source><year>2004</year><volume>113</volume><fpage>285</fpage><lpage>294</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsuruoka</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsuruoka</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name>